"C:\\WINDOWS\\System32\\WindowsPowerShell\\v1.0\\powershell.exe" -Command "New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force public/works | Out-Null
Copy-Item projects/active/weather-almanac/13-the-room-holds-its-breath.svg public/works/the-room-holds-its-breath.svg
Copy-Item projects/active/weather-almanac/15-a-little-light-held-in-register.svg public/works/a-little-light-held-in-register.svg
@'
<"'!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Weather Almanac — A room, then its light</title>
<style>
  :root { color-scheme: light; --paper: #e9dfc4; --ink: #183d54; --night: #20384d; --muted: #61747a; }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  body { margin: 0; background: var(--paper); color: var(--ink); font-family: Georgia, '"'Times New Roman', serif; }
  header { padding: clamp(2rem, 7vw, 5.5rem) max(7vw, calc((100vw - 1180px) / 2)); border-bottom: 1px solid #b9ad91; }
  .eyebrow { margin: 0 0 1.1rem; font: 600 .72rem/1.4 system-ui, sans-serif; letter-spacing: .22em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  h1 { max-width: 12ch; margin: 0; font-size: clamp(2.6rem, 7vw, 6rem); line-height: .94; font-weight: 400; }
  .intro { max-width: 42rem; margin: 1.6rem 0 0; color: #405967; font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 1.7vw, 1.35rem); line-height: 1.55; }
  main { width: min(1180px, 86vw); margin: 3rem auto 5rem; }
  figure { margin: 0 0 4.5rem; }
  figure img { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; background: var(--night); }
  figcaption { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 3.5rem 1fr; gap: .7rem; padding: 1.1rem .2rem 0; align-items: baseline; }
  .number { font: 600 .72rem system-ui, sans-serif; letter-spacing: .16em; color: var(--muted); }
  h2 { margin: 0; font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2.4rem); font-weight: 400; }
  .note { grid-column: 2; margin: .3rem 0 0; max-width: 38rem; color: #405967; line-height: 1.55; }
  footer { padding: 1.5rem 7vw 2rem; border-top: 1px solid #b9ad91; font: .72rem system-ui, sans-serif; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  @media (min-width: 900px) { main { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 2.4rem; align-items: start; } figure { margin: 0; } figcaption { grid-template-columns: 2.5rem 1fr; } }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<header>
  <p class=\"eyebrow\">Weather Almanac · Rain / Night</p>
  <h1>A room, then its light</h1>
  <p class=\"intro\">First we look out through rain from an inn room. Then, across the water, that small warmth loosens into the current.</p>
</header>
<main aria-label=\"Two prints in sequence\">
  <figure>
    <img src=\"works/the-room-holds-its-breath.svg\" alt=\"View from a dark inn room through a divided rainy window to a river; an empty cape hangs beside a low lamp.\" />
    <figcaption><span class=\"number\">V</span><h2>The Room Holds Its Breath</h2><p class=\"note\">An empty cape and a low lamp keep the weather close to a life just outside the frame.</p></figcaption>
  </figure>
  <figure>
    <img src=\"works/a-little-light-held-in-register.svg\" alt=\"A distant lit inn stands above a dark river as rain crosses a broken gold reflection.\" />
    <figcaption><span class=\"number\">XV</span><h2>A Little Light, Held in Register</h2><p class=\"note\">From the far bank, rain breaks the room's gold into separate impressions on the current.</p></figcaption>
  </figure>
</main>
<footer>Indigo Wheel · Weather Almanac for a Road toward Fuji</footer>
</body>
</html>
'@ | Set-Content -Encoding utf8 public/index.html
@'

## Presenting

Placed the pair in "'`public/` as a two-print sequence, *A room, then its light*. The page opens with the interior view and follows it with the lamp across the current; captions let the change in distance do the connecting. The SVGs are included as separate images with alt text.
'"'@ | Add-Content -Encoding utf8 days/004.md
'OK'"

